# Finite integer search qualification tool

Root executed this observer against the actual public route_admitted call in batch27-routing-search. Admission, fixtures, canonical token checks and snapshots precede counters/timing; search consumes the original token, callback and spent guard once. Successful outputs are checked independently for canonical borrowed IDs, exact anchors, orthogonality, open-rectangle clearance and collapsed collinearity after measurement.

The fixed job records ten unchanged-default groups (32/64/128/256/1024 nodes, densities 1/2), each with two warmups and seven measurements. Admission Work/Nodes refusals explicitly have search_called=false and null search metrics. Four separate controls cover default Grid refusal, lowered-to-already-spent work quota, pre-call cancellation and cancellation on search poll 3 after axis reservation. Five malformed CLI cases require exit 2. Wrong outcomes, OOM and timeouts remain failures; there is no fallback or default-limit relaxation.

The allocator is an immutable source dependency from #183 commit 337433fb18a377e2f1a4c12fe5510b2d0798cfdb: C09/batch26-routing-admission-profile/u11a_profile.rs, Git blob 2f38d0e92afb48815ab813b8c887d760b887856d, whole SHA-256 36127a02052ca203cead039dc2dae82e5e77118686ccf1d34c6d6f33bb1a0dda. Before compilation the driver checks the whole bytes/blob and unchanged lines 12–95, block SHA-256 1f927e4d0a780666081a13b4bdc4d2f3ffb94f220ac9bf39cdea8162734e3eb3, then writes an exclusive private include and binds original/generated bytes before and after compilation/execution. This reuses existing published logic; all new extraction/include/verification code counts as authored production. Initial live includes the admitted token; consumed frees remain in signed net delta. Requested traffic, absolute/new phase peak and process VmHWM differ; VmHWM includes admission/setup. summarize.py reports separate seven-sample min/max ranges with raw-input hashes and no pooled p95. The oversized formatted 417-line observer remains immutable pre-reuse provenance, not an executed or accepted implementation.

Outer attempts 01 and 02 refused their respective 8 GiB and 7 GiB host minima before any scope, compilation or profiling; exact source and raw receipts remain preserved. Attempt 03 was never executed and remains a separate source-only epoch without a resource receipt. Independently reviewed experimental outer attempt 04 uses two CPUs, memory high 1 GiB/max 1536 MiB, no swap, 128 tasks, fresh host minimum 5.5 GiB (5,767,168 KiB) and unchanged 180/660/720-second child/outer/scope bounds. This retains the 4 GiB arithmetic host margin. The #193 standard-library compile fits 1 GiB; attempt 04 subsequently completed this release build and search profile within the experimental frame, without establishing a capacity guarantee. Attempt 03 created neither inner output nor target 01; attempt 04 then created and used both. OOM, nonzero exits, timeouts and wrong case outcomes remain failures, with no fallback, quota increase or foreign-process intervention.

The frame hash-loads the shared ownership helper from #184, attests the actual invocation and controls, and preserves proof-bound cleanup, raw failures and before/after bindings. The inner job owns the nonblocking compiler lock and builds one offline locked release graph with serde_json 1.0.151. verify_routing.py is the exact root-owned 96-line library checker for the refreshed current-main composition; its execution/receipt belongs to the separate U11b qualification packet. Root executed the release/profile jobs; source authors executed only data assembly. Native ELK, fractional geometry, connected UI, p95 and successful-capacity acceptance remain OPEN.
